  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual claim and the visual representation of political figures",
  "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto any deictic element like 'me', 'you', or 'your...'. However, the meme's structure and intent create an implicit projection where the user is positioned as a viewer interpreting the satirical claim. The user is projected onto the textual material ('president trump has suggested random drug tests be performed on members of congress') and the visual material (Nancy Pelosi, Chuck Schumer, and the Black woman speaker) as the subjects of the claim. The user is expected to understand the meme's satirical framing, which implies a shared understanding of political discourse and the meme's intent to mock the proposal by associating it with the depicted figures. This projection is onto the scene as a whole, where the user is invited to interpret the juxtaposition of text and image as a commentary on political figures.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
